#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Accurately calculating chemical reaction energies is crucial for scientific "
"advancements in materials science, chemical engineering, drug discovery, and"
" other fields. Among various chemical systems, the Li-S system has garnered "
"significant interest for understanding and developing new battery "
"compositions. This tutorial provides hands-on experience in calculating the "
"Li-S bond dissociation potential energy surface (PES) of a $Li_2S$ system by"
" removing one lithium atom using HI-VQE calculations. You can compare the "
"results with reference calculations (CASCI) and with classical methods such "
"as Hartree-Fock (HF) for a 20-qubit problem.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The lithium-sulfur example connects this workflow to research on next-"
"generation batteries for energy storage. Calculating how energy changes as a"
" Li-S bond breaks provides molecular-level insight relevant to understanding"
" the chemical transformations in these systems. More broadly, potential "
"energy surfaces are tools for studying reaction pathways and catalysts for "
"more resource-efficient chemical processes.\n"
msgstr ""

